1
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:50,319
Come over to my place right now.

2
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,280
And kneel right outside my door!

3
00:01:51,640 --> 00:01:53,239
I really can't make it today.

4
00:01:53,719 --> 00:01:54,640
So you're not going to help Eldest Brother?

5
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:55,640
Of course I have to help!

6
00:01:55,879 --> 00:01:56,599
And besides,

7
00:01:56,599 --> 00:01:57,640
over what happened with Eldest Brother,

8
00:01:58,359 --> 00:02:00,159
The old man and Sister-in-law are livid!

9
00:02:00,159 --> 00:02:01,200
Don't I need to step in and stop them?

10
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,159
What are they arguing about?

11
00:02:03,599 --> 00:02:05,200
About Eldest Brother going to Jinli Palace...

12
00:02:05,680 --> 00:02:07,120
It seems the old man called the police.

13
00:02:11,280 --> 00:02:11,960
Wait, hold on a second.

14
00:02:13,280 --> 00:02:13,680
Eldest Brother...

15
00:02:14,439 --> 00:02:16,120
The old man called the cops on him at Jinli Palace?

16
00:02:17,319 --> 00:02:18,800
What kind of mess is this?

17
00:02:19,120 --> 00:02:20,360
Y-You better explain this to me!

18
00:02:20,360 --> 00:02:21,520
What the hell happened? Spell it out!

19
00:02:21,919 --> 00:02:22,759
That's why

20
00:02:22,759 --> 00:02:24,080
I definitely can't make it tonight.

21
00:02:24,639 --> 00:02:25,719
It's just a house!

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:26,800
I'll find you another one.

23
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:27,400
Find what?

24
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:28,960
My entire place is already packed up!

25
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:29,919
Where am I supposed to put my stuff?

26
00:02:30,120 --> 00:02:31,080
You sold the place,

27
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:31,479
so what am I supposed to do?

28
00:02:31,479 --> 00:02:32,000
All right, all right.

29
00:02:32,240 --> 00:02:33,120
Sounds like they're at it again over here.

30
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:33,800
I've got to go break them up.

31
00:02:33,919 --> 00:02:34,960
Gotta hang up. I'll talk to you tomorrow.

32
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:37,280
Tell me,

33
00:02:38,319 --> 00:02:39,520
is anyone in your family reliable at all?

34
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:05,639
Uncle!

35
00:03:06,719 --> 00:03:07,240
Uncle!

36
00:03:09,759 --> 00:03:10,280
Uncle!

37
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,400
I see your car's outside.

38
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,400
Are you in, Uncle?

39
00:03:18,560 --> 00:03:19,199
Qingyou.

40
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:19,879
Uncle.

41
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:21,120
Last night...

42
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,639
the supervisor got locked up.

43
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:23,560
The supervisor?

44
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:26,240
Locked up where?

45
00:03:27,280 --> 00:03:27,960
At the police station.

46
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,199
The old supervisor was hauled in.

47
00:03:30,439 --> 00:03:30,960
You didn't know?

48
00:03:31,319 --> 00:03:32,000
I had no idea.

49
00:03:32,800 --> 00:03:33,479
Come sit down. Have a seat.

50
00:03:33,479 --> 00:03:34,800
Tell me what happened.

51
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:35,479
What... what happened?

52
00:03:35,879 --> 00:03:36,800
Last night,

53
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:39,280
Brother Xiuming and the supervisor were hauled in together.

54
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:40,199
You didn't know about that either?

55
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:42,360
Our eldest got locked up too?

56
00:03:42,840 --> 00:03:43,919
I had no clue!

57
00:03:46,240 --> 00:03:47,080
Uncle, are you really...

58
00:03:47,520 --> 00:03:48,560
No, wait, hold on.

59
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:52,520
Yesterday I specifically told you to accompany him.

60
00:03:53,039 --> 00:03:54,439
How did our eldest end up inside?

61
00:03:55,159 --> 00:03:55,599
Uncle,

62
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:57,280
what happened last night,

63
00:03:57,879 --> 00:04:00,319
nine times out of ten it was my sister-in-law's idea.

64
00:04:00,560 --> 00:04:01,639
She's trying to snatch the job from me.

65
00:04:01,879 --> 00:04:02,719
Without my sister-in-law,

66
00:04:03,439 --> 00:04:04,240
would my big bro even dare?

67
00:04:05,080 --> 00:04:05,879
No, no.

68
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:06,919
Something else doesn't add up.

69
00:04:07,639 --> 00:04:08,560
Last night,

70
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:09,639
didn't I call you?

71
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,479
I asked if you'd reached Jinli Palace.

72
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:12,719
You told me you were there.

73
00:04:13,439 --> 00:04:14,360
You didn't go.

74
00:04:14,360 --> 00:04:15,479
Why did you say you were there?

75
00:04:15,520 --> 00:04:17,319
Wasn't it because I was afraid you'd get mad?

76
00:04:17,480 --> 00:04:18,759
If you got mad,

77
00:04:18,759 --> 00:04:19,720
you'd chew out Brother Xiuming again,

78
00:04:19,720 --> 00:04:20,720
and make it look like I was snitching on him.

79
00:04:21,879 --> 00:04:22,279
Uncle,

80
00:04:23,639 --> 00:04:25,759
why do you care so much if I went or not?

81
00:04:25,759 --> 00:04:26,399
Whether I went or not...

82
00:04:26,600 --> 00:04:27,920
if I'd actually gone last night,

83
00:04:27,920 --> 00:04:29,040
wouldn't I be the one locked up now?

84
00:04:30,279 --> 00:04:31,319
What's that supposed to mean?

85
00:04:31,319 --> 00:04:32,680
Were you trying to get me thrown in jail?

86
00:04:33,519 --> 00:04:34,120
Yang Qingyou!

87
00:04:34,759 --> 00:04:36,319
Is that how you talk to your uncle?!

88
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:38,439
Let's just be honest.

89
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:39,480
Uncle,

90
00:04:39,759 --> 00:04:41,800
yesterday I bawled my eyes out,

91
00:04:41,800 --> 00:04:42,920
pouring my heart out to you for so long,

92
00:04:43,319 --> 00:04:44,680
and you didn't believe me at all.

93
00:04:44,759 --> 00:04:45,279
In... get inside.

94
00:04:45,319 --> 00:04:46,399
Wait, what am I going inside for?

95
00:04:46,560 --> 00:04:47,199
What are you doing?

96
00:04:47,199 --> 00:04:47,560
Get inside!

97
00:04:47,879 --> 00:04:48,399
Get the hell inside!

98
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:48,959
Wait, you—

99
00:04:48,959 --> 00:04:49,240
Inside!

100
00:04:49,240 --> 00:04:50,639
You told me to go to Jinli Palace...

101
00:04:50,639 --> 00:04:51,000
Inside!

102
00:04:51,040 --> 00:04:52,439
You had this planned all along, didn't you?

103
00:04:52,439 --> 00:04:53,040
Get inside!

104
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:54,800
You just wanted to get me locked up, didn't you?!

105
00:04:55,120 --> 00:04:55,439
Sit down!

106
00:04:56,279 --> 00:04:56,600
No, look...

107
00:04:56,839 --> 00:04:59,680
You and Brother Xiuming are at odds too.

108
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,240
You're both just watching your backs.

109
00:05:01,399 --> 00:05:01,680
I—

110
00:05:07,800 --> 00:05:08,680
Morning, Second Brother.

111
00:05:08,920 --> 00:05:09,480
What are you playing at?

112
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,639
Showing up right when we're leaving for work...

113
00:05:10,639 --> 00:05:11,759
Afraid we'd chew you out, aren't you?

114
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,000
Morning, Second Sister-in-law.

115
00:05:13,879 --> 00:05:14,920
About yesterday, I'm really sorry.

116
00:05:14,959 --> 00:05:15,480
I came over to apologize.

117
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,519
Get a move on today.

118
00:05:16,879 --> 00:05:17,680
We have to move in the next couple of days.

119
00:05:17,680 --> 00:05:18,720
Hear me out about yesterday's apartment.

120
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:19,720
Did you hear me? Hurry up!

121
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:20,639
I'm talking to Second Sister-in-law.

122
00:05:21,040 --> 00:05:21,720
That apartment...

123
00:05:22,040 --> 00:05:22,720
Listen to me.

124
00:05:22,759 --> 00:05:24,160
I knew you wouldn't want it.

125
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:25,399
Take a look at this one.

126
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:26,360
130 square meters.

127
00:05:26,439 --> 00:05:27,000
With an elevator.

128
00:05:27,160 --> 00:05:27,720
In a good school district.

129
00:05:27,759 --> 00:05:28,399
What now?

130
00:05:29,079 --> 00:05:29,720
One cut wasn't enough for you?

131
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,879
Now you want agency fees too?

132
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:32,079
That really hurts to hear.

133
00:05:32,319 --> 00:05:33,439
I'm giving you the insider rate.

134
00:05:33,639 --> 00:05:34,279
Seriously, take a look.

135
00:05:34,279 --> 00:05:34,920
No, no, not looking!

136
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:35,279
Just take a look.

137
00:05:35,279 --> 00:05:35,639
No.

138
00:05:36,439 --> 00:05:37,439
Give it back. Let him take it.

139
00:05:37,439 --> 00:05:38,519
I'm talking to her. You're not in charge.

140
00:05:38,519 --> 00:05:39,680
I just want that 120-square-meter place.

141
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:40,519
It was move-in ready!

142
00:05:40,519 --> 00:05:41,480
Don't push me to tell the truth.

143
00:05:42,639 --> 00:05:43,120
Fine, fine, fine.

144
00:05:43,240 --> 00:05:43,839
Tell the truth, then.

145
00:05:43,879 --> 00:05:45,040
Let's hear what you've got to say. Come on.

146
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:46,680
Out with it.

147
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:49,240
Fine.

148
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:50,160
Second Brother...

149
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:53,680
Downsizing to a smaller place...

150
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,480
and dragging my sister-in-law down too?

151
00:05:55,680 --> 00:05:56,800
How we choose to live

152
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:57,600
is our own business.

153
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:58,160
What's it to you?

154
00:05:58,160 --> 00:05:59,279
That compound is terrible, too.

155
00:05:59,439 --> 00:06:01,399
And it's far from both of your jobs.

156
00:06:01,439 --> 00:06:02,879
Don't think I don't know what you're up to.

157
00:06:03,720 --> 00:06:04,319
Fine, go on.

158
00:06:04,519 --> 00:06:05,040
Tell us.

159
00:06:05,120 --> 00:06:06,079
What are we up to?

160
00:06:06,199 --> 00:06:06,600
I'm listening.

161
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:07,639
Flipping!

162
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:08,959
Renting!

163
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:10,519
That's my line of work.

164
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:12,279
You think you can fool me?

165
00:06:12,519 --> 00:06:13,360
"Nowhere to live"?

166
00:06:13,360 --> 00:06:14,319
You think I'd buy that?

167
00:06:14,319 --> 00:06:15,000
Then tell me,

168
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:16,600
where are we supposed to live?

169
00:06:16,920 --> 00:06:17,560
How should I know?

170
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,120
Maybe the old man bought you two a new place.

171
00:06:20,319 --> 00:06:21,519
Cut the crap, Old Three.

172
00:06:21,519 --> 00:06:22,959
Look at all this stuff!

173
00:06:22,959 --> 00:06:23,399
Just look at it!

174
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:24,639
All my and your sister-in-law's stuff,

175
00:06:24,639 --> 00:06:25,480
where are we supposed to put it?

176
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:25,839
Keep acting.

177
00:06:25,839 --> 00:06:27,040
We don't even have a place to sleep!

178
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:27,680
Do you get that?

179
00:06:28,079 --> 00:06:29,319
Playing the victim won't work on me.

180
00:06:29,319 --> 00:06:29,800
If you want to play the victim,

181
00:06:29,800 --> 00:06:30,879
go cry to the old man!

182
00:06:30,879 --> 00:06:31,639
Play the victim?

183
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:32,399
Why would we play the victim with you?

184
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,360
Sister-in-law,

185
00:06:34,639 --> 00:06:36,560
don't play innocent after cashing in.

186
00:06:36,639 --> 00:06:38,720
Everyone knows the old man favors Old Two.

187
00:06:38,959 --> 00:06:39,879
With that demolition contract,

188
00:06:39,879 --> 00:06:41,319
he took Old Two along to negotiate.

189
00:06:41,639 --> 00:06:43,319
The old man just got the compensation payout,

190
00:06:43,439 --> 00:06:45,439
and now you're downsizing your apartment?

191
00:06:45,519 --> 00:06:46,839
Does that make any sense?

192
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:48,480
Just look at your wedding back then.

193
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:49,240
That banquet...

194
00:06:49,439 --> 00:06:51,000
you wished you could host it at City Hall.

195
00:06:51,240 --> 00:06:52,680
Now you've learned to endure hardship?

196
00:06:53,040 --> 00:06:54,079
Old Two roughing it, sure, I'd buy that.

197
00:06:54,240 --> 00:06:55,600
But a pampered princess like you?

198
00:06:55,759 --> 00:06:56,399
No way.

199
00:06:56,680 --> 00:06:58,079
So what's your angle here?

200
00:06:58,079 --> 00:06:58,879
Here's my take:

201
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:00,279
Either the old man

202
00:07:00,279 --> 00:07:01,319
bought you a new place,

203
00:07:01,639 --> 00:07:02,519
or what else could it be?

204
00:07:02,600 --> 00:07:03,199
A pity play.

205
00:07:03,279 --> 00:07:04,240
It's called playing the victim!

206
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,480
You want him to feel sorry for you

207
00:07:05,480 --> 00:07:06,800
and squeeze some cash out of him.

208
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:07,759
Am I right or am I right?

209
00:07:07,759 --> 00:07:08,560
Instead of talking bullshit here,

210
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,800
why don't you get the apartment back for me?

211
00:07:09,800 --> 00:07:10,600
That's the easiest way.

212
00:07:10,600 --> 00:07:11,120
I'm telling the truth.

213
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:12,000
Your second brother is quitting his job.

214
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:15,519
He's starting his own law firm.

215
00:07:16,199 --> 00:07:16,839
We have no money.

216
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:18,639
We sold the place to free up cash.

217
00:07:19,199 --> 00:07:19,720
Satisfied now?

218
00:07:27,839 --> 00:07:28,480
I didn't catch that.

219
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,000
Just now, she said...

220
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,639
She said hurry up and get the house back.

221
00:07:32,439 --> 00:07:33,360
Sai Xiuhe, let me tell you something.

222
00:07:34,199 --> 00:07:35,639
Scheme against whoever you want, however you want.

223
00:07:35,639 --> 00:07:36,319
It has nothing to do with me.

224
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:38,800
But if you fling mud at me again,

225
00:07:39,199 --> 00:07:40,439
it won't end as easily as today.

226
00:07:42,680 --> 00:07:43,000
Why, you...

227
00:07:44,519 --> 00:07:45,439
I'm staying at a hotel.

228
00:07:47,040 --> 00:07:47,800
Honey, you're staying at a hotel?

229
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:48,879
Where... where am I supposed to stay?

230
00:07:49,399 --> 00:07:50,399
Stay at your law firm!

231
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,480
Isn't that brand-new too?

232
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:58,399
Yang Qingyou.

233
00:07:59,000 --> 00:07:59,800
Do you really think

234
00:08:00,800 --> 00:08:02,560
if I wanted to get you locked up,

235
00:08:03,480 --> 00:08:05,920
I'd have to frame you at Jinli Palace?

236
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:08,600
You thought the tricks

237
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:09,879
you pulled in our account books...

238
00:08:10,079 --> 00:08:10,720
I didn't know about them?

239
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:13,040
You really think I've gone senile?

240
00:08:13,360 --> 00:08:15,000
Back when I ran construction crews,

241
00:08:15,639 --> 00:08:17,040
you were still running around in diapers.

242
00:08:17,399 --> 00:08:18,319
Every little trick you know,

243
00:08:18,319 --> 00:08:19,480
didn't I teach it to you?

244
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:20,120
Am I right?

245
00:08:20,240 --> 00:08:20,519
Right.

246
00:08:21,160 --> 00:08:21,519
Wait, no...

247
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,720
I took pity on you

248
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:26,000
having no real father.

249
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,560
Right? So I let it slide.

250
00:08:28,879 --> 00:08:30,519
I trusted you so much,

251
00:08:30,600 --> 00:08:31,279
and after all this time,

252
00:08:31,279 --> 00:08:34,080
I spent ten years raising a backstabber!

253
00:08:34,919 --> 00:08:35,960
You really trusted me?

254
00:08:36,320 --> 00:08:37,000
If you trusted me,

255
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,519
would you audit the books behind my back?

256
00:08:39,799 --> 00:08:41,919
Not being blood means you're never family.

257
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,840
You never believed in me from the start!

258
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:45,200
Blood?

259
00:08:46,399 --> 00:08:48,679
Before your dad got that demolition payout,

260
00:08:49,799 --> 00:08:51,519
you didn't treat him as your real father?

261
00:08:52,039 --> 00:08:53,279
Now he gets demolition money,

262
00:08:53,279 --> 00:08:54,679
clutching a few dirty bucks,

263
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:56,480
and overnight he's your real dad!

264
00:08:57,480 --> 00:08:59,240
You eat my food,

265
00:08:59,679 --> 00:09:00,679
poach my crew,

266
00:09:00,919 --> 00:09:01,799
and steal my business!

267
00:09:02,200 --> 00:09:03,679
If you're going to play like that,

268
00:09:04,879 --> 00:09:06,639
then let's lay everything on the line!

269
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,200
We'll take the books,

270
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:11,320
the books from the past decade,

271
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:12,639
and audit every line!

272
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:13,600
If things don't balance,

273
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:15,960
you cough up every single cent!

274
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:17,679
And if you can't cough it up,

275
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,960
my second son studied law,

276
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:20,679
as you well know.

277
00:09:20,879 --> 00:09:22,320
We'll handle this through the legal system!

278
00:09:23,240 --> 00:09:25,240
I'll march in and file a police report,

279
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,080
and the court will definitely take it!

280
00:09:27,639 --> 00:09:28,360
Once the case is opened...

281
00:09:28,360 --> 00:09:28,759
Uncle!

282
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:29,639
Uncle!

283
00:09:30,759 --> 00:09:32,039
I was wrong! I was wrong!

284
00:09:32,120 --> 00:09:33,639
Please don't call the police!

285
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:35,279
Don't take it to court, Uncle!

286
00:09:35,960 --> 00:09:38,639
For the sake of our bond all these years,

287
00:09:40,320 --> 00:09:41,919
please give me another chance, will you?

288
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:43,799
I'll confess!

289
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:44,919
It's my dad...

290
00:09:45,200 --> 00:09:46,840
He set up a construction crew of his own,

291
00:09:47,240 --> 00:09:48,080
and asked me to go work with him.

292
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:50,320
Uncle, I was wrong! I was really wrong!

293
00:09:50,559 --> 00:09:51,279
The only reason I came

294
00:09:51,279 --> 00:09:53,159
was specifically to apologize to you!

295
00:09:53,279 --> 00:09:53,879
Get up.

296
00:09:53,879 --> 00:09:54,440
I was wrong.

297
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,399
I'll never do it again!

298
00:09:55,399 --> 00:09:56,240
Get up and talk.

299
00:09:57,519 --> 00:09:58,159
Get up.

300
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,679
I was wrong, Uncle.

301
00:10:00,039 --> 00:10:01,200
I'll never dare to do it again!

302
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:02,799
You're quitting, then?

303
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:12,480
Are you out of your mind?

304
00:10:13,159 --> 00:10:14,919
You might as well just stab the old man!

305
00:10:15,320 --> 00:10:16,039
It's not that bad.

306
00:10:16,039 --> 00:10:16,919
Not that bad?

307
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:19,200
You're the first college graduate in Qingyangli!

308
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:21,159
And the old man got you into the Port Authority—

309
00:10:21,159 --> 00:10:22,200
do you know how much effort that took?

310
00:10:22,320 --> 00:10:24,240
You're the blessing rising from the Sai family graves!

311
00:10:24,240 --> 00:10:24,720
You know that?

312
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:25,960
My dear Second Brother!

313
00:10:26,200 --> 00:10:27,399
What were you thinking?

314
00:10:27,679 --> 00:10:28,360
Aside from anything else,

315
00:10:28,840 --> 00:10:29,840
for the Sai family,

316
00:10:30,039 --> 00:10:31,039
emotionally,

317
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:31,960
financially,

318
00:10:31,960 --> 00:10:32,799
and for our reputation,

319
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:34,519
you've screwed up big time!

320
00:10:34,679 --> 00:10:35,600
This isn't even just a screw-up.

321
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:36,720
You tore a hole right through the sky!

322
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:38,240
The sky is falling, you know that?

323
00:10:38,399 --> 00:10:38,799
Third Brother.

324
00:10:39,279 --> 00:10:40,200
Resigning is my business.

325
00:10:40,679 --> 00:10:42,000
Once I find my footing,

326
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:43,399
I'll tell the old man myself.

327
00:10:43,559 --> 00:10:44,519
This has nothing to do with you.

328
00:10:44,519 --> 00:10:45,000
Stay out of it.

329
00:10:45,279 --> 00:10:46,440
All you need to do

330
00:10:46,440 --> 00:10:47,559
is keep your mouth shut.

331
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:48,960
Pretend you don't know a thing.

332
00:10:50,360 --> 00:10:51,000
Can you do that?

333
00:10:57,879 --> 00:10:58,320
Second Brother,

334
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,120
I'll do it,

335
00:11:02,320 --> 00:11:03,320
but on one condition.

336
00:11:03,399 --> 00:11:03,799
Name it.

337
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:05,639
How much money did the old man get?

338
00:11:10,399 --> 00:11:11,080
About that...

339
00:11:12,279 --> 00:11:14,240
Don't ask me. I don't know!

340
00:11:15,960 --> 00:11:16,919
Don't play dumb with me.

341
00:11:18,559 --> 00:11:20,039
I'll give you one more chance, Second Brother.

342
00:11:20,039 --> 00:11:21,440
Give me as many as you want,

343
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,519
I just don't know!

344
00:11:22,519 --> 00:11:23,399
Stop asking me!

345
00:11:23,399 --> 00:11:24,080
Sai Xiuliang,

346
00:11:25,159 --> 00:11:26,720
don't force me to call the old man.

347
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:28,759
Last chance.

348
00:11:28,799 --> 00:11:30,440
How much money did the old man get?

349
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:32,159
What's that supposed to mean?

350
00:11:33,879 --> 00:11:34,960
Third Brother, are you threatening me?

351
00:11:35,639 --> 00:11:36,559
You're barely wet behind the ears,

352
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:37,519
and you dare threaten me?

353
00:11:37,559 --> 00:11:38,639
What are you thinking?

354
00:11:39,039 --> 00:11:40,440
You think I'm scared of you calling the old man,

355
00:11:40,440 --> 00:11:41,120
or what?

356
00:11:41,399 --> 00:11:42,639
You think you can scare me with that?

357
00:11:44,600 --> 00:11:45,360
Go on, call him!

358
00:11:45,879 --> 00:11:46,840
Come on, Sai Xiuhe, call him right now!

359
00:11:46,840 --> 00:11:48,120
If you don't call the old man,

360
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:48,879
you're a coward!

361
00:11:48,879 --> 00:11:49,559
Call him right now!

362
00:11:49,879 --> 00:11:50,600
Do you even know,

363
00:11:50,840 --> 00:11:51,519
if you call the old man,

364
00:11:51,519 --> 00:11:52,320
what he's gonna say?

365
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,120
You don't, do you?

366
00:11:53,159 --> 00:11:54,000
Let me tell you.

367
00:11:54,440 --> 00:11:55,159
The old man will say,

368
00:11:55,159 --> 00:11:56,360
"Sai Xiuhe, what is wrong with you?

369
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,360
Your brother is resigning,

370
00:11:57,360 --> 00:11:58,360
why didn't you stop him?

371
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,559
Why are you snitching on your own brother?

372
00:11:59,759 --> 00:12:01,120
Why are you only telling me now?"

373
00:12:08,759 --> 00:12:09,320
One thousand,

374
00:12:10,039 --> 00:12:10,559
four hundred,

375
00:12:10,679 --> 00:12:11,279
and twenty-eight.

376
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,639
If we calculate it,

377
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:20,799
at your birth dad Yang the Second's place,

378
00:12:20,919 --> 00:12:21,960
the demolition money

379
00:12:21,960 --> 00:12:23,679
would easily come out to

380
00:12:24,360 --> 00:12:25,039
around nine million.

381
00:12:25,279 --> 00:12:26,840
There are three in his family,

382
00:12:27,240 --> 00:12:28,120
plus you,

383
00:12:28,440 --> 00:12:29,799
that makes four.

384
00:12:30,559 --> 00:12:31,960
If it's split evenly,

385
00:12:33,879 --> 00:12:36,200
you could get around two million.

386
00:12:36,399 --> 00:12:37,720
You're pulling my leg.

387
00:12:38,879 --> 00:12:40,159
Don't you know my situation?

388
00:12:40,559 --> 00:12:42,639
My dad gave me to his brother as a kid.

389
00:12:43,200 --> 00:12:44,120
Then my uncle

390
00:12:44,399 --> 00:12:45,360
went and had a son of his own.

391
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,480
The demolition money goes to his son.

392
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:48,159
He told me,

393
00:12:48,639 --> 00:12:49,840
"If you want a cut,

394
00:12:49,919 --> 00:12:50,919
go ask your dad."

395
00:12:51,480 --> 00:12:52,440
So I went to my dad,

396
00:12:52,559 --> 00:12:53,120
and my dad said,

397
00:12:53,240 --> 00:12:54,679
"You were adopted by your uncle.

398
00:12:54,679 --> 00:12:55,679
Go ask him for it.

399
00:12:55,679 --> 00:12:57,159
Your household registry isn't with me."

400
00:12:57,279 --> 00:12:57,679
So...

401
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,440
none of that money is coming to me.

402
00:12:59,639 --> 00:13:00,799
Cut the nonsense.

403
00:13:00,799 --> 00:13:01,480
Just tell me:

404
00:13:01,480 --> 00:13:02,519
this money,

405
00:13:02,559 --> 00:13:04,000
this two million or so in compensation,

406
00:13:04,039 --> 00:13:05,159
do you want it or not?

407
00:13:05,519 --> 00:13:06,399
Are you going to give it to me?

408
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:10,039
Well, I... I just don't have that kind of luck, Uncle.

409
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:10,360
Do you want it,

410
00:13:11,799 --> 00:13:12,519
or don't you?

411
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:32,919
How does it feel?

412
00:13:34,679 --> 00:13:35,440
How should I put it?

413
00:13:36,120 --> 00:13:36,879
Anyway...

414
00:13:37,039 --> 00:13:38,039
It's a real rush, unlike the Port Authority.

415
00:13:38,159 --> 00:13:38,519
What about you?

416
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:39,480
I feel nothing.

417
00:13:40,399 --> 00:13:41,320
Nothing at all?

418
00:13:41,600 --> 00:13:43,480
Like everything is just gone.

419
00:13:45,639 --> 00:13:46,720
There you go being gloomy again.

420
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,440
Our law firm hasn't even opened yet.

421
00:13:49,480 --> 00:13:50,279
Besides,

422
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:51,759
with our expertise,

423
00:13:52,039 --> 00:13:53,000
are you worried we won't get cases?

424
00:13:53,679 --> 00:13:55,480
By the way, look into Tengyue Group for me.

425
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,759
Their smart terminal project is up for bid.

426
00:13:58,919 --> 00:14:00,279
I heard they're

427
00:14:00,279 --> 00:14:02,240
looking for long-term legal outsourcing.

428
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:03,840
And they specifically want a local firm.

429
00:14:04,279 --> 00:14:04,879
What?

430
00:14:05,519 --> 00:14:06,080
Brother-in-law,

431
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:08,120
ever heard of aiming out of our league?

432
00:14:08,960 --> 00:14:10,519
Even if we submitted our profile,

433
00:14:10,519 --> 00:14:12,279
they'd toss it in the trash after a look.

434
00:14:12,600 --> 00:14:13,600
How many firms have you seen

435
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:14,799
succeed just by handing in paperwork?

436
00:14:15,879 --> 00:14:16,600
So what do you plan to do?

437
00:14:16,879 --> 00:14:18,919
Also, their new boss, Shi Yongnian.

438
00:14:19,919 --> 00:14:21,519
His resume, background,

439
00:14:21,559 --> 00:14:22,840
working style, preferences...

440
00:14:22,840 --> 00:14:23,840
The more detailed, the better.

441
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:24,519
Dig it all up for me.

442
00:14:24,840 --> 00:14:25,120
Wait,

443
00:14:25,559 --> 00:14:26,799
you just said he's new here.

444
00:14:26,799 --> 00:14:27,879
How am I supposed to look into him?

445
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:28,279
Dad,

446
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:29,600
are you free?

447
00:14:29,879 --> 00:14:30,840
Hurry up and come back home.

448
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:32,440
Uncle,

449
00:14:33,440 --> 00:14:34,600
can my second brother make it?

450
00:14:35,639 --> 00:14:36,399
With one word from me,

451
00:14:36,960 --> 00:14:37,639
would he dare not show up?

452
00:14:38,879 --> 00:14:39,320
Qingyou,

453
00:14:40,200 --> 00:14:42,200
are you completely sure about this?

454
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:44,159
If you take the money,

455
00:14:45,080 --> 00:14:46,399
then this family...

456
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:47,639
you can never come back.

457
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,759
I've made up my mind. I'm sure.

458
00:14:50,519 --> 00:14:51,799
Just go all out, Uncle.

459
00:14:54,120 --> 00:14:54,639
Yang the Second.

460
00:14:55,480 --> 00:14:55,960
I'm right here.

461
00:14:56,879 --> 00:14:57,320
Let's both

462
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:58,759
have a little chat.

463
00:14:58,919 --> 00:14:59,799
Chat about what?

464
00:15:00,080 --> 00:15:00,879
Haven't we talked enough?

465
00:15:00,960 --> 00:15:01,879
Is this a soap opera?

466
00:15:02,159 --> 00:15:02,759
I have nothing to say to you.

467
00:15:03,080 --> 00:15:03,519
Please leave.

468
00:15:04,919 --> 00:15:07,120
Seeing as we're from the same village,

469
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,639
I'm sparing you the embarrassment.

470
00:15:09,399 --> 00:15:10,799
If you want to save face,

471
00:15:10,919 --> 00:15:11,799
we can talk things through nicely.

472
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:14,080
But if you keep being sarcastic,

473
00:15:14,519 --> 00:15:16,159
don't blame me for getting rough.

474
00:15:16,279 --> 00:15:16,879
Who are you cursing at?

475
00:15:16,879 --> 00:15:17,679
Who's the shameless one here?

476
00:15:17,759 --> 00:15:18,440
This isn't your house.

477
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:20,600
Go strut around in your own home

478
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:22,080
and boss people around to get your kicks.

479
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:23,279
How dare you come to my place?

480
00:15:23,399 --> 00:15:23,960
Get out of here right now.

481
00:15:24,080 --> 00:15:24,919
I don't have time for you.

482
00:15:25,039 --> 00:15:25,600
Head on out.

483
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:26,279
Out you go.

484
00:15:26,360 --> 00:15:26,639
Get out.

485
00:15:26,799 --> 00:15:28,240
Keep moving. Out!

486
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,480
You, come inside first.

487
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:31,639
Yang Qingyou, get in here.

488
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:34,759
Dad...

489
00:15:35,279 --> 00:15:36,320
This is your son.

490
00:15:36,320 --> 00:15:36,960
You recognize him, right?

491
00:15:37,360 --> 00:15:40,240
He embezzled and cooked my crew's books.

492
00:15:40,360 --> 00:15:41,240
And I caught him.

493
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:41,639
Uncle...

494
00:15:41,799 --> 00:15:42,080
Shut up!

495
00:15:42,080 --> 00:15:42,360
Uncle...

496
00:15:43,399 --> 00:15:44,840
I was going to call the police.

497
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:47,399
Only because we're from the same village,

498
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:48,600
I came to give you a heads-up.

499
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:49,600
What do you think we should do?

500
00:15:49,919 --> 00:15:50,240
Wait...

501
00:15:57,639 --> 00:15:57,960
Call them!

502
00:15:58,159 --> 00:15:58,799
Call the police right now!

503
00:15:58,879 --> 00:15:59,559
You have to call!

504
00:15:59,759 --> 00:16:00,279
I'm telling you,

505
00:16:00,399 --> 00:16:01,039
if the son breaks the law,

506
00:16:01,039 --> 00:16:01,840
it's got nothing to do with the father!

507
00:16:01,919 --> 00:16:02,559
Call 110!

508
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:03,279
Call right now!

509
00:16:03,559 --> 00:16:03,879
You,

510
00:16:03,960 --> 00:16:04,799
get out with him!

511
00:16:05,240 --> 00:16:05,639
Get out!

512
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,399
What are you laughing at?

513
00:16:06,480 --> 00:16:07,000
Go! Get moving!

514
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:07,480
Go call the police!

515
00:16:07,480 --> 00:16:07,879
Put justice before family!

516
00:16:07,879 --> 00:16:08,159
Hurry up and go!

517
00:16:08,519 --> 00:16:08,799
What are you doing?

518
00:16:08,799 --> 00:16:09,080
Move!

519
00:16:09,360 --> 00:16:09,799
What are you doing?

520
00:16:09,879 --> 00:16:10,320
Get out!

521
00:16:10,320 --> 00:16:10,759
Let go of me!

522
00:16:10,759 --> 00:16:11,159
Get the hell out!

523
00:16:11,159 --> 00:16:12,440
Uncle, let's stop arguing, okay?

524
00:16:12,440 --> 00:16:13,000
Shut up!

525
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:13,879
We're done talking about this!

526
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:14,360
You...

527
00:16:14,519 --> 00:16:14,919
Move!

528
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:15,679
That's enough, that's enough!

529
00:16:15,679 --> 00:16:16,759
Are you going to leave or not?

530
00:16:16,759 --> 00:16:17,559
Wanna get physical?

531
00:16:18,360 --> 00:16:20,039
Check if you can afford it first.

532
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:21,200
Gang fighting,

533
00:16:21,279 --> 00:16:23,039
intentional assault, provoking trouble...

534
00:16:23,039 --> 00:16:23,919
you'll catch every single charge!

535
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:24,399
What,

536
00:16:24,399 --> 00:16:25,559
wanna go back inside for a few more years?

537
00:16:25,679 --> 00:16:26,120
Who's going inside?

538
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:26,600
You!

539
00:16:26,720 --> 00:16:27,559
If anyone's going inside, it's you!

540
00:16:27,799 --> 00:16:28,559
This is my home!

541
00:16:28,639 --> 00:16:29,519
This is my private residence!

542
00:16:29,519 --> 00:16:30,039
Who told you this is a private residence?

543
00:16:30,039 --> 00:16:30,720
All right, that's enough!

544
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:31,840
Everyone, let go!

545
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,600
We're all from the same village!

546
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:35,240
Can't we talk this out reasonably?

547
00:16:35,279 --> 00:16:36,519
Don't get physical!

548
00:16:36,759 --> 00:16:37,440
Bring over a couple of stools!

549
00:16:38,240 --> 00:16:39,200
Sit down and talk it through!

550
00:16:43,519 --> 00:16:44,039
I'll go myself.

551
00:16:44,120 --> 00:16:44,879
Don't go, it'll just upset you.

552
00:16:45,320 --> 00:16:46,279
Why shouldn't I go?

553
00:16:46,399 --> 00:16:47,600
Your eldest brother was wrongly accused,

554
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:48,240
he's been through so much.

555
00:16:48,519 --> 00:16:49,840
Now that his name is finally cleared,

556
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:52,679
I need to properly thank the police.

557
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:03,879
Sai Duoxi!

558
00:17:04,079 --> 00:17:05,440
Don't think I don't know

559
00:17:05,440 --> 00:17:06,000
what you're scheming in that petty gut!

560
00:17:06,519 --> 00:17:08,039
Isn't it because I signed the crew

561
00:17:08,039 --> 00:17:09,000
and took your business,

562
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,559
so you're using him to spite me?

563
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:16,799
Yang Qingyou embezzled money.

564
00:17:17,039 --> 00:17:17,839
Prison time alone won't cut it.

565
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:19,119
He has to return the money and compensate.

566
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,079
Where did all that embezzled money go?

567
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:23,240
You father and son have been very close lately,

568
00:17:23,559 --> 00:17:24,440
making quite a splash,

569
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:25,519
and taking on so many projects.

570
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,400
Where did that money come from?

571
00:17:26,599 --> 00:17:27,160
That was my dem...

572
00:17:27,519 --> 00:17:28,480
My demolition compensation!

573
00:17:28,799 --> 00:17:29,640
That's your claim.

574
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:30,559
You're free to present evidence.

575
00:17:30,880 --> 00:17:32,039
Gather evidence and call the police anytime.

576
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:33,640
But once we're in court,

577
00:17:34,039 --> 00:17:35,200
it's not just whatever you say it is.

578
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:37,079
Let me school you on the law.

579
00:17:37,200 --> 00:17:39,000
First, your accounts will be frozen,

580
00:17:39,359 --> 00:17:40,400
until the court finishes its investigation.

581
00:17:41,039 --> 00:17:42,440
That could be fast, or it could be slow.

582
00:17:42,720 --> 00:17:43,359
If it's fast,

583
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:44,160
six to ten months.

584
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:45,039
If it's slow,

585
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,359
three to five years is entirely possible.

586
00:17:47,119 --> 00:17:48,680
In short, until everything is cleared up,

587
00:17:49,279 --> 00:17:50,640
will your bank accounts

588
00:17:50,640 --> 00:17:51,519
be back in normal use.

589
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:51,920
Fr...

590
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:52,599
Have I made myself clear?

591
00:17:52,839 --> 00:17:53,640
Freeze? But I...

592
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:56,200
I just fronted money for two job sites!

593
00:17:56,599 --> 00:17:57,480
If you freeze my accounts,

594
00:17:58,079 --> 00:17:59,200
aren't you ruining me?!

595
00:17:59,319 --> 00:17:59,799
Yang Er!

596
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:02,559
You two, father and son,

597
00:18:02,880 --> 00:18:04,880
teamed up to ruin me!

598
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:05,359
You know that?!

599
00:18:05,599 --> 00:18:07,759
One embezzled my money on the inside,

600
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,240
and the other stole my business on the outside!

601
00:18:10,480 --> 00:18:11,279
Let me tell you,

602
00:18:12,359 --> 00:18:13,720
every single loss I suffer,

603
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:14,880
you will pay for it!

604
00:18:20,759 --> 00:18:21,839
Don't get physical! Hands off!

605
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:24,000
Director, this has nothing to do with me!

606
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,119
He was adopted out a long time ago!

607
00:18:25,480 --> 00:18:26,079
Whatever he does,

608
00:18:26,079 --> 00:18:27,240
how can it be blamed on me?

609
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:28,279
Duoxi,

610
00:18:29,319 --> 00:18:30,359
you're a reasonable man.

611
00:18:30,759 --> 00:18:33,359
Can't we find a way that works for everyone?

612
00:18:33,359 --> 00:18:34,880
Don't push this to mutual destruction,

613
00:18:34,880 --> 00:18:35,559
all right?

614
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:36,480
Director...

615
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:38,240
There's no other way.

616
00:18:38,480 --> 00:18:40,319
We have to play by the rules.

617
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:46,000
Over here!

618
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:46,680
Xiuhe!

619
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:47,279
Brother, brother!

620
00:18:47,279 --> 00:18:47,960
Sorry for the trouble, really sorry.

621
00:18:47,960 --> 00:18:48,720
I really caused you so much trouble.

622
00:18:49,440 --> 00:18:49,880
You're out.

623
00:18:59,000 --> 00:18:59,960
I... I mean...

624
00:19:00,400 --> 00:19:01,519
Honestly, I really didn't...

625
00:19:02,960 --> 00:19:03,519
Hurry up.

626
00:19:03,799 --> 00:19:04,240
How humiliating.

627
00:19:07,400 --> 00:19:07,880
Get in the back.

628
00:19:09,160 --> 00:19:10,119
If I were you, I'd just sit in the back.

629
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,039
All right, Sister-in-law.

630
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,200
Don't stay mad.

631
00:19:23,680 --> 00:19:24,559
We all know deep down

632
00:19:24,559 --> 00:19:25,519
what this is really about.

633
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:27,279
If you're angry,

634
00:19:27,279 --> 00:19:28,359
go take it out on the old man back home!

635
00:19:28,640 --> 00:19:30,200
Don't bully my eldest brother here.

636
00:19:31,880 --> 00:19:33,000
How come you suddenly

637
00:19:33,519 --> 00:19:34,480
know how to talk sense?

638
00:19:35,880 --> 00:19:36,319
Big Brother,

639
00:19:36,839 --> 00:19:37,759
I'm not trying to stir up trouble,

640
00:19:38,240 --> 00:19:39,039
but if I were you,

641
00:19:39,079 --> 00:19:40,880
I couldn't swallow this insult today.

642
00:19:41,079 --> 00:19:42,200
Go back and flip the table on the old man!

643
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:43,640
Ask him what the hell is going on.

644
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:44,720
Lay down the terms,

645
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:45,799
and spill everything out.

646
00:19:46,319 --> 00:19:47,240
That's more like it.

647
00:19:47,359 --> 00:19:48,680
That's the real Sai Xiuhe:

648
00:19:49,359 --> 00:19:51,119
ranting, instigating, a real shit-stirrer.

649
00:19:53,640 --> 00:19:54,720
Sister-in-law, Big Brother,

650
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:57,039
I actually understand you both completely.

651
00:19:57,519 --> 00:19:57,960
I get it.

652
00:19:58,119 --> 00:19:59,920
You rely on the old man's crew

653
00:19:59,920 --> 00:20:01,200
to put food on your table.

654
00:20:01,440 --> 00:20:02,160
Now it's different.

655
00:20:02,799 --> 00:20:04,200
An opportunity is right in front of you.

656
00:20:05,039 --> 00:20:06,400
The demolition payout has come through.

657
00:20:07,160 --> 00:20:08,640
Big Brother, Crown Prince,

658
00:20:08,920 --> 00:20:10,400
your chance to rise up has finally arrived.

659
00:20:11,160 --> 00:20:12,559
You sure thought it all out for us.

660
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:14,319
Then why don't you teach us:

661
00:20:14,799 --> 00:20:15,440
how do we rise up?

662
00:20:15,559 --> 00:20:16,039
Just two words:

663
00:20:17,039 --> 00:20:17,400
Split the money.

664
00:20:18,480 --> 00:20:19,160
Third Brother Sai,

665
00:20:19,759 --> 00:20:20,720
you say that in front of me,

666
00:20:20,720 --> 00:20:21,720
and I'll pretend I didn't hear it.

667
00:20:22,440 --> 00:20:23,480
Don't you dare go blabbing outside

668
00:20:23,480 --> 00:20:24,680
and making a fool of our family.

669
00:20:25,200 --> 00:20:26,359
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

670
00:20:26,359 --> 00:20:27,519
The elders are still alive and well,

671
00:20:27,519 --> 00:20:28,839
and you already want to split the estate!

672
00:20:29,079 --> 00:20:29,559
Just... just...

673
00:20:29,559 --> 00:20:31,119
So neither of you knows

674
00:20:31,119 --> 00:20:33,759
the family got 14,280,000?

675
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:36,960
I...

676
00:20:37,799 --> 00:20:38,160
I...

677
00:20:40,599 --> 00:20:41,559
H-How much?

678
00:20:42,079 --> 00:20:43,400
"The elders are still alive and well"?

679
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:44,799
Now, this money...

680
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:45,839
are we splitting it or not?

681
00:20:51,480 --> 00:20:51,880
Director,

682
00:20:53,279 --> 00:20:54,279
there is one way.

683
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:55,720
We just need Yang Qingyou

684
00:20:56,839 --> 00:20:57,960
to cough up all the dirty money,

685
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:58,960
cover the entire deficit,

686
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,359
and then have my father

687
00:21:00,680 --> 00:21:02,000
issue a letter of understanding.

688
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,200
Qingyou said

689
00:21:03,559 --> 00:21:04,759
he doesn't have the money.

690
00:21:04,920 --> 00:21:06,359
He gave all of it to Yang the Second.

691
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:07,400
What money does he have?

692
00:21:07,839 --> 00:21:08,759
That's my money!

693
00:21:09,359 --> 00:21:10,640
He was given up for adoption!

694
00:21:11,000 --> 00:21:12,440
Let his other father clean up his mess!

695
00:21:12,960 --> 00:21:14,119
Yang the Second,

696
00:21:14,240 --> 00:21:16,400
you'd really rather die than pay up.

697
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:19,240
Even if you can abandon your own son,

698
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,680
if the court freezes your accounts,

699
00:21:21,839 --> 00:21:22,680
all that money of yours...

700
00:21:22,839 --> 00:21:24,119
won't it all be frozen anyway?

701
00:21:24,440 --> 00:21:25,279
If you keep this up,

702
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:27,079
you... you'll just live to regret it.

703
00:21:27,759 --> 00:21:29,920
You'll live to regret it, understand?

704
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:36,240
Fine.

705
00:21:36,480 --> 00:21:37,480
I'm not wasting my breath on this anymore.

706
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:37,960
Let's go.

707
00:21:38,119 --> 00:21:38,519
Go, move!

708
00:21:39,599 --> 00:21:39,880
Get out.

709
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:40,359
Let's go!

710
00:21:43,279 --> 00:21:44,000
Fine!

711
00:21:45,920 --> 00:21:46,400
I'll split it.

712
00:21:49,519 --> 00:21:50,680
I'll give you the money!

713
00:21:54,960 --> 00:21:55,559
Yang Qingyou!

714
00:21:56,839 --> 00:21:57,640
Starting today,

715
00:21:59,160 --> 00:22:00,559
I'm no longer your father!

716
00:22:01,559 --> 00:22:02,519
If you and Sai Duoxi

717
00:22:02,519 --> 00:22:03,839
get into any more shady business,

718
00:22:03,839 --> 00:22:04,880
don't you dare come looking for me!

719
00:22:05,839 --> 00:22:06,599
You mark my words!

720
00:22:07,400 --> 00:22:08,960
Yang Qingyou, I'm not your father!

721
00:22:10,319 --> 00:22:11,440
I don't have a son like you!

722
00:22:12,440 --> 00:22:13,160
If anything happens down the road,

723
00:22:14,079 --> 00:22:14,599
don't come to me!

724
00:22:14,599 --> 00:22:15,200
Go to the police!

725
00:22:27,039 --> 00:22:28,480
Did you hear me?

726
00:22:29,680 --> 00:22:30,440
I heard you.

727
00:22:30,920 --> 00:22:32,000
I heard you.

728
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:34,680
From now on,

729
00:22:35,279 --> 00:22:36,400
my life is my own.

730
00:22:36,759 --> 00:22:37,920
I won't drag you down.

731
00:22:38,480 --> 00:22:40,039
A demolition payout,

732
00:22:40,799 --> 00:22:42,519
a real father and son.

733
00:22:43,359 --> 00:22:44,720
Things ended up like this.

734
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:46,200
In theory,

735
00:22:46,839 --> 00:22:47,480
nothing's wrong.

736
00:22:48,440 --> 00:22:49,559
But in your heart,

737
00:22:50,400 --> 00:22:50,799
it's just not right.

738
00:22:51,440 --> 00:22:52,599
Who won and who lost,

739
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:54,960
nobody can say.

740
00:22:57,400 --> 00:22:57,720
All right.

741
00:22:58,200 --> 00:22:59,279
Let's call this matter settled.

742
00:22:59,279 --> 00:22:59,519
Fine.

743
00:22:59,759 --> 00:23:00,240
I'll get back to work.

744
00:23:00,240 --> 00:23:00,960
Head on back. Go on.

745
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:02,240
Uncle.

746
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:05,039
Thank you.

747
00:23:05,359 --> 00:23:06,279
Don't thank me.

748
00:23:06,559 --> 00:23:07,799
Now that you've severed ties with your dad,

749
00:23:08,079 --> 00:23:10,160
just work hard and stick with me.

750
00:23:10,920 --> 00:23:11,319
Here, take this.

751
00:23:11,599 --> 00:23:12,440
Head home for now.

752
00:23:13,559 --> 00:23:13,960
Lao Er.

753
00:23:16,200 --> 00:23:16,599
Lao Er.

754
00:23:20,799 --> 00:23:22,240
What've you been busy with lately?

755
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:23,880
Something urgent came up at work.

756
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:24,799
They want me to head back.

757
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:25,279
Overtime.

758
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:26,680
I wanted to talk to you.

759
00:23:27,119 --> 00:23:28,839
I want to expand our construction team,

760
00:23:29,079 --> 00:23:30,359
make it bigger,

761
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:32,440
get more workers and machinery.

762
00:23:33,039 --> 00:23:33,519
Sure.

763
00:23:34,119 --> 00:23:35,160
Expand it if you want.

764
00:23:35,519 --> 00:23:36,200
As long as you're happy.

765
00:23:37,559 --> 00:23:38,759
I'm not finished talking.

766
00:23:39,359 --> 00:23:40,799
What's your wife up to?

767
00:23:40,880 --> 00:23:42,319
Why hasn't she visited in over six months?

768
00:23:42,319 --> 00:23:43,279
Tell her to come visit.

769
00:23:43,279 --> 00:23:44,079
Well, she...

770
00:23:44,359 --> 00:23:45,279
she's busy at the TV station.

771
00:23:45,359 --> 00:23:45,799
She can't get away.

772
00:23:46,039 --> 00:23:47,519
She's well into her thirties.

773
00:23:48,079 --> 00:23:49,799
It's time she had a baby.

774
00:23:50,200 --> 00:23:52,240
You've been married for almost ten years.

775
00:23:52,640 --> 00:23:54,680
No kids makes us a neighborhood joke.

776
00:23:55,079 --> 00:23:56,839
They can't even wipe their own asses.

777
00:23:56,839 --> 00:23:57,920
As if they have time to laugh at us.

778
00:23:58,119 --> 00:23:58,640
Besides,

779
00:23:59,119 --> 00:24:00,440
all you talk about is having a baby.

780
00:24:00,519 --> 00:24:01,680
Who's going to raise it?

781
00:24:01,839 --> 00:24:02,279
Stop worrying about it.

782
00:24:02,279 --> 00:24:03,240
You stubborn kid, still talking back.

783
00:24:21,119 --> 00:24:22,200
You walk around every day

784
00:24:22,680 --> 00:24:24,000
with that beat-up bag under your arm.

785
00:24:24,720 --> 00:24:25,559
Can't you get a new one?

786
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:27,920
I'm embarrassed for you.

787
00:24:28,119 --> 00:24:28,960
Are you jealous?

788
00:24:29,880 --> 00:24:30,480
Do you even have one?

789
00:24:30,759 --> 00:24:31,519
Damn right.

790
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,039
Wherever I take this bag,

791
00:24:33,039 --> 00:24:34,559
people look up to me.

792
00:24:34,680 --> 00:24:35,240
When there's a project,

793
00:24:35,359 --> 00:24:36,680
they give it to me, not you.

794
00:24:37,440 --> 00:24:38,400
When it's time to get paid,

795
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:39,720
I'm ahead of you in line.

796
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:40,279
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

797
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:40,839
Right?

798
00:24:40,839 --> 00:24:41,599
You're amazing.

799
00:24:41,920 --> 00:24:43,319
And your son is even more amazing.

800
00:24:43,319 --> 00:24:43,920
By the way,

801
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:48,039
you really drink wherever you go.

802
00:24:48,880 --> 00:24:49,640
You bet.

803
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:50,319
Say,

804
00:24:51,319 --> 00:24:51,759
in a little bit,

805
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:54,400
are you playing good cop or bad cop?

806
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:56,480
What do you mean?

807
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,079
So I know how to back you up.

808
00:25:15,440 --> 00:25:15,880
Old Wei.

809
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:16,440
I'm here, I'm here.

810
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:17,279
Come on, hurry in.

811
00:25:17,839 --> 00:25:18,480
Have a seat.

812
00:25:18,480 --> 00:25:19,240
Take a seat, take a seat.

813
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:19,519
Sit down.

814
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:20,559
You're late.

815
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,400
Yeah, what kept you?

816
00:25:22,559 --> 00:25:23,960
Just got back from North Village.

817
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:25,440
Went to check out a project.

818
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:26,559
You're a busy man.

819
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:28,599
Busier than the mayor.

820
00:25:29,480 --> 00:25:30,079
For real.

821
00:25:30,640 --> 00:25:31,759
Look, about... about...

822
00:25:32,400 --> 00:25:33,319
Xizi and me...

823
00:25:33,720 --> 00:25:34,440
The phase two payment...

824
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:35,839
When will it come through?

825
00:25:36,119 --> 00:25:37,240
I've already pushed for it.

826
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:39,119
Just wait a bit longer.

827
00:25:40,640 --> 00:25:41,160
Old Wei,

828
00:25:41,319 --> 00:25:43,799
you sent your wife and kid abroad,

829
00:25:43,799 --> 00:25:45,000
and one of these days,

830
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:46,160
you might just pack up and leave.

831
00:25:46,200 --> 00:25:47,599
Don't keep using new projects

832
00:25:47,599 --> 00:25:48,640
to feed us empty promises.

833
00:25:48,839 --> 00:25:50,359
Let's talk about what's in front of us.

834
00:25:50,640 --> 00:25:51,759
Before Mid-Autumn Festival,

835
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:53,119
can the phase two payment come through?

836
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:53,599
Xizi,

837
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:55,440
we've known each other over twenty years.

838
00:25:55,599 --> 00:25:56,720
When have I ever shortchanged you two?

839
00:25:56,720 --> 00:25:57,400
Right, right.

840
00:25:57,799 --> 00:25:59,000
Do a solid job,

841
00:25:59,279 --> 00:26:00,359
get it through inspection quickly,

842
00:26:00,680 --> 00:26:02,319
and you won't miss out on a dime.

843
00:26:02,319 --> 00:26:03,319
Sure, sure.

844
00:26:04,279 --> 00:26:05,160
The way you make it sound,

845
00:26:05,160 --> 00:26:07,640
it's like we've just been freeloading off you.

846
00:26:07,960 --> 00:26:10,480
Over the years, you took contracts from Tengyue Group

847
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:12,279
and subcontracted them to us.

848
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,279
We've never skimped on your cut, have we?

849
00:26:15,400 --> 00:26:16,480
Every single time,

850
00:26:16,759 --> 00:26:18,559
your payouts were delayed,

851
00:26:18,759 --> 00:26:20,680
but our cuts to you were never short.

852
00:26:21,039 --> 00:26:21,880
Look at you whining.

853
00:26:22,319 --> 00:26:23,799
Acting all self-righteous now, are you?

854
00:26:24,279 --> 00:26:26,200
Am I holding onto this money

855
00:26:26,200 --> 00:26:27,279
and refusing to pay you?

856
00:26:27,440 --> 00:26:28,200
Let me tell you,

857
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:29,359
if it weren't for me,

858
00:26:29,519 --> 00:26:30,920
could you two have even landed this project?

859
00:26:31,200 --> 00:26:31,759
That's true.

860
00:26:32,559 --> 00:26:32,960
Old Wei,

861
00:26:33,480 --> 00:26:35,279
don't push us around with that talk.

862
00:26:35,559 --> 00:26:36,880
If you push us too far,

863
00:26:36,960 --> 00:26:38,160
we'll just go get ourselves

864
00:26:38,319 --> 00:26:39,319
a construction qualification,

865
00:26:39,400 --> 00:26:40,480
and start our own company.

866
00:26:41,079 --> 00:26:41,319
Why, you...

867
00:26:43,039 --> 00:26:43,599
Xi-zi, Xi-zi.

868
00:26:44,119 --> 00:26:46,519
It's easy watching others carry the load.

869
00:26:47,119 --> 00:26:48,400
Once you actually do it, you'll know...

870
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:49,599
just how tough it really is.

871
00:26:49,680 --> 00:26:51,599
There's a whole lot of tricks to it.

872
00:26:51,599 --> 00:26:52,359
Exactly.

873
00:26:52,359 --> 00:26:53,519
What tricks? Why don't you tell me?

874
00:26:53,519 --> 00:26:54,119
Come on, Xi-zi.

875
00:26:54,319 --> 00:26:55,440
Stop talking nonsense.

876
00:26:55,839 --> 00:26:56,920
How old are you now?

877
00:26:57,039 --> 00:26:58,039
Only wear shoes

878
00:26:58,200 --> 00:26:58,960
that fit your feet.

879
00:26:59,039 --> 00:27:00,279
Stop taking sides here.

880
00:27:00,880 --> 00:27:02,680
Don't... Don't you want that money?

881
00:27:03,039 --> 00:27:04,559
Who said I didn't want it?

882
00:27:04,759 --> 00:27:05,920
See?

883
00:27:06,200 --> 00:27:07,960
But... watch your tone.

884
00:27:08,559 --> 00:27:10,039
Then how should I speak?

885
00:27:10,119 --> 00:27:10,319
Fine.

886
00:27:10,319 --> 00:27:10,640
You tell me.

887
00:27:11,119 --> 00:27:12,000
How would I know?

888
00:27:12,119 --> 00:27:12,960
All right, that's enough.

889
00:27:12,960 --> 00:27:14,599
Stop putting on a double act, you two.

890
00:27:15,200 --> 00:27:16,279
And Old Ma, I see...

891
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:17,920
can't keep it up anymore, right?

892
00:27:18,079 --> 00:27:19,119
Not at all.

893
00:27:19,319 --> 00:27:19,839
Look, Xi-zi.

894
00:27:20,440 --> 00:27:21,599
Let's talk about you.

895
00:27:21,799 --> 00:27:22,960
With this demolition payout,

896
00:27:23,039 --> 00:27:23,880
how much extra did you get?

897
00:27:24,559 --> 00:27:25,839
You got at least...

898
00:27:26,200 --> 00:27:27,519
three or four million more than me.

899
00:27:27,680 --> 00:27:28,319
Am I right?

900
00:27:28,400 --> 00:27:28,920
Nonsense.

901
00:27:29,039 --> 00:27:29,440
No way.

902
00:27:29,839 --> 00:27:30,319
I didn't.

903
00:27:30,319 --> 00:27:31,119
That's impossible.

904
00:27:31,240 --> 00:27:32,880
With so many people registered in your household...

905
00:27:33,039 --> 00:27:33,319
All right.

906
00:27:33,759 --> 00:27:34,759
Enough, stop prying already.

907
00:27:35,039 --> 00:27:37,039
Tell us about your money.

908
00:27:37,240 --> 00:27:38,039
What are your plans for it?

909
00:27:38,960 --> 00:27:40,240
For... for my family, it's simple.

910
00:27:40,799 --> 00:27:42,559
An equal share for me and my two sons.

911
00:27:42,839 --> 00:27:44,440
My daughter moved back in after her divorce.

912
00:27:45,319 --> 00:27:46,920
But as long as she lives with me,

913
00:27:47,240 --> 00:27:48,279
I'll provide for her.

914
00:27:48,720 --> 00:27:50,640
Everyone can chip in to help her out.

915
00:27:50,839 --> 00:27:51,720
And that'll settle it.

916
00:27:51,799 --> 00:27:52,240
Old Ma.

917
00:27:52,480 --> 00:27:53,640
You just got this money,

918
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:54,240
and you're already dividing it up?

919
00:27:54,480 --> 00:27:55,759
Should I just hoard it in my hands?

920
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:56,799
At my age,

921
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:58,279
can I take it to the grave?

922
00:27:58,720 --> 00:27:59,359
Dacheng.

923
00:28:00,079 --> 00:28:00,960
Let me give you some advice.

924
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:02,640
This money...

925
00:28:03,440 --> 00:28:04,160
you can't divide it.

926
00:28:06,039 --> 00:28:06,920
Why can't we split it?

927
00:28:07,279 --> 00:28:08,720
You can't sort it out.

928
00:28:10,839 --> 00:28:12,039
Sister-in-law, about this money,

929
00:28:12,039 --> 00:28:13,079
we still have to split it.

930
00:28:13,079 --> 00:28:14,240
The money is just sitting there right now.

931
00:28:14,440 --> 00:28:15,519
Why shouldn't we divide it?

932
00:28:15,799 --> 00:28:16,440
Can't all of us

933
00:28:16,440 --> 00:28:17,759
take the money and live well?

934
00:28:18,039 --> 00:28:18,440
Think about Zhenzhu.

935
00:28:18,440 --> 00:28:19,119
Someone's here.

936
00:28:19,799 --> 00:28:20,240
Who is it?

937
00:28:23,119 --> 00:28:24,079
Uncle's not home?

938
00:28:24,519 --> 00:28:24,960
He's not here.

939
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:25,799
Nobody's home?

940
00:28:26,839 --> 00:28:27,200
Sister-in-law.

941
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:28,759
What's all this about?

942
00:28:29,279 --> 00:28:31,799
Uncle Duoxi wants to invest at our union.

943
00:28:32,039 --> 00:28:32,319
So, you see...

944
00:28:32,440 --> 00:28:34,440
we brought over the free gifts first,

945
00:28:34,559 --> 00:28:35,920
just to show our sincerity.

946
00:28:36,160 --> 00:28:36,519
Thank you.

947
00:28:36,559 --> 00:28:36,960
Just a small token of goodwill.

948
00:28:36,960 --> 00:28:37,559
Big Brother, take this bag of rice.

949
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:38,480
You're too kind.

950
00:28:39,440 --> 00:28:40,519
My dad wants to invest?

951
00:28:41,039 --> 00:28:41,759
Let's talk inside. Come in.

952
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:42,640
It's not finalized yet.

953
00:28:43,039 --> 00:28:44,480
We've been waiting for Uncle's answer.

954
00:28:44,480 --> 00:28:45,079
Please come in. Come on in.

955
00:28:45,079 --> 00:28:45,319
All right!

956
00:28:45,559 --> 00:28:46,160
How much is he investing?

957
00:28:46,319 --> 00:28:46,799
Lao San,

958
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:47,839
put in a good word with Uncle

959
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:48,599
about the product I pitched to him.

960
00:28:48,599 --> 00:28:49,240
Wait, wait, wait.

961
00:28:49,480 --> 00:28:50,279
Let me say something first.

962
00:28:50,440 --> 00:28:50,880
Give me a second.

963
00:28:50,920 --> 00:28:51,440
Wait for what?

964
00:28:51,559 --> 00:28:51,960
Just get in here. Come on.

965
00:28:51,960 --> 00:28:53,079
Come on, they're already here.

966
00:28:53,079 --> 00:28:53,880
Come inside. Come on in!

967
00:28:54,680 --> 00:28:56,119
Big Brother, he can't invest!

968
00:28:56,279 --> 00:28:57,559
If he invests, there's no money to split!

969
00:28:57,799 --> 00:28:59,400
You... you return their gifts right now!

970
00:28:59,799 --> 00:29:00,119
Lao San!

971
00:29:00,599 --> 00:29:01,519
Is this your call to make?

972
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:02,799
Doesn't Dad get to decide?

973
00:29:03,039 --> 00:29:04,160
Take it up with your sister-in-law.

974
00:29:04,519 --> 00:29:05,079
Come on, come on.

975
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:05,759
Let's talk inside. Come in.

976
00:29:05,920 --> 00:29:06,279
Come on in.

977
00:29:06,519 --> 00:29:07,319
They're waiting for Dad!

978
00:29:07,319 --> 00:29:07,680
No, no.

979
00:29:07,680 --> 00:29:08,400
Let's... let's talk inside.

980
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:09,000
All right.

981
00:29:09,480 --> 00:29:11,279
I told you not to bring it in! Hey!

982
00:29:11,279 --> 00:29:11,559
Stop!

983
00:29:11,559 --> 00:29:12,480
It's just a small token of our sincerity.

984
00:29:17,759 --> 00:29:18,039
Well,

985
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:19,400
Jiayin

986
00:29:20,079 --> 00:29:21,279
went out of her way to bring

987
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:22,920
this Northeast rice over.

988
00:29:23,279 --> 00:29:23,559
Step over it.

989
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:28,400
What happened to Big Brother?

990
00:29:30,440 --> 00:29:31,079
Mind your own business.

991
00:29:31,960 --> 00:29:32,480
Stop prying.

992
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:33,319
Take it off.

993
00:29:35,319 --> 00:29:35,640
Isn't that inappropriate?

994
00:29:35,640 --> 00:29:36,039
Take it off!

995
00:29:41,440 --> 00:29:42,000
They haven't left.

996
00:29:42,359 --> 00:29:42,680
They haven't left.

997
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,119
All right, that's enough.

998
00:29:44,079 --> 00:29:44,599
We'll keep the rice.

999
00:29:44,599 --> 00:29:45,240
We can't take this, though.

1000
00:29:45,400 --> 00:29:46,279
My dad really doesn't buy investments.

1001
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:46,799
Thanks for coming by.

1002
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:47,759
Wait, Lao San.

1003
00:29:47,880 --> 00:29:48,880
This is just a small token of our appreciation.

1004
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:49,799
To show our sincerity.

1005
00:29:50,160 --> 00:29:51,200
Just keep it, whether he buys or not.

1006
00:29:51,920 --> 00:29:52,400
Goodbye, goodbye.

1007
00:30:07,880 --> 00:30:08,200
Brother-in-law.

1008
00:30:08,319 --> 00:30:09,799
This is all the information we could find.

1009
00:30:13,119 --> 00:30:14,000
It's about to start. Go on ahead.

1010
00:30:14,359 --> 00:30:14,640
All right.

1011
00:30:23,039 --> 00:30:23,319
Come on over.

1012
00:30:23,920 --> 00:30:24,559
Xiao Xu is here.

1013
00:30:24,880 --> 00:30:25,200
Xiao Yuan.

1014
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:26,839
Mr. Shi, let me introduce you.

1015
00:30:27,119 --> 00:30:28,400
Director Yuan from the Bidding Office.

1016
00:30:28,880 --> 00:30:29,960
Mr. Shi, welcome, welcome.

1017
00:30:32,119 --> 00:30:32,519
Chief Song.

1018
00:30:32,839 --> 00:30:33,920
This is Mr. Shi from Tengyue.

1019
00:30:34,839 --> 00:30:35,799
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

1020
00:30:35,799 --> 00:30:36,720
Hello, hello, hello.

1021
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:37,839
Welcome, welcome, welcome.

1022
00:30:38,599 --> 00:30:39,680
Let's talk in the conference room.

1023
00:30:39,839 --> 00:30:40,119
Sounds good.

1024
00:30:41,240 --> 00:30:42,319
Hello, colleagues.

1025
00:30:42,519 --> 00:30:44,279
Welcome, everyone,

1026
00:30:44,559 --> 00:30:45,599
to Honggang City's

1027
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:47,480
Smart Terminal

1028
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:48,880
Tender Briefing.

1029
00:30:49,200 --> 00:30:50,440
Now, let me introduce

1030
00:30:50,960 --> 00:30:53,319
the three bidding companies

1031
00:30:53,720 --> 00:30:54,880
and the colleagues attending.

1032
00:30:54,960 --> 00:30:56,759
Rongsheng Group, Colleague Cheng Shihai.

1033
00:31:00,680 --> 00:31:02,480
Sanhui Building, Colleague Cao Xianshui.

1034
00:31:05,799 --> 00:31:08,200
Tengyue Property, Colleague Shi Yongnian.

1035
00:31:24,119 --> 00:31:25,000
What are you doing? I...

1036
00:31:25,400 --> 00:31:26,480
Haven't I already explained it?

1037
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:28,359
I really didn't do anything.

1038
00:31:28,599 --> 00:31:29,519
I went to treat him to dinner,

1039
00:31:29,519 --> 00:31:31,279
how would I know there was an afterparty?

1040
00:31:31,599 --> 00:31:32,440
When he said he wanted to go,

1041
00:31:32,440 --> 00:31:33,759
wasn't I supposed to take him?

1042
00:31:34,079 --> 00:31:34,799
Besides,

1043
00:31:35,039 --> 00:31:35,559
taking him out to dinner,

1044
00:31:35,559 --> 00:31:37,160
wasn't it you who told me to take him? I...

1045
00:31:37,160 --> 00:31:38,079
How many times is this now?

1046
00:31:38,400 --> 00:31:39,240
The first time.

1047
00:31:39,720 --> 00:31:40,640
It's honestly my first time.

1048
00:31:40,640 --> 00:31:41,440
Otherwise, when the cops walked in,

1049
00:31:41,440 --> 00:31:42,000
why would I have bolted?

1050
00:31:42,000 --> 00:31:42,759
I'm asking you,

1051
00:31:42,960 --> 00:31:43,880
in front of your father,

1052
00:31:43,880 --> 00:31:45,079
how many times have you chickened out?

1053
00:31:46,000 --> 00:31:47,039
What do you mean, "chickened out"?

1054
00:31:50,720 --> 00:31:51,640
You think you just had bad luck?

1055
00:31:52,200 --> 00:31:53,559
Your dad snitched on you!

1056
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:55,559
Your dad called the cops to arrest you!

1057
00:31:55,559 --> 00:31:56,519
How can you still not get it?

1058
00:31:56,519 --> 00:31:57,559
What kind of nonsense are you talking?

1059
00:31:57,680 --> 00:31:58,480
My dad turned me in?

1060
00:31:58,680 --> 00:31:59,519
I'm his own flesh and blood!

1061
00:31:59,799 --> 00:32:01,319
Throw me into the police station?

1062
00:32:01,680 --> 00:32:02,519
That's utter bullshit!

1063
00:32:02,640 --> 00:32:04,079
I heard Yang Qingyou yell it with my own ears!

1064
00:32:04,319 --> 00:32:05,559
Your dad didn't deny it. Why?

1065
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:06,599
Because he did it!

1066
00:32:06,920 --> 00:32:08,000
You got locked up,

1067
00:32:08,079 --> 00:32:08,759
and look at him!

1068
00:32:08,960 --> 00:32:10,200
Eating and drinking like normal,

1069
00:32:10,200 --> 00:32:10,920
like nothing even happened!

1070
00:32:11,359 --> 00:32:12,559
He plays the great patriarch,

1071
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:14,000
while you act like his pathetic dog!

1072
00:32:14,240 --> 00:32:15,640
Because you're useless with no backbone!

1073
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:16,119
You're a coward!

1074
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:18,000
That's why they walk all over us,

1075
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:19,000
pushing us around like this!

1076
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:19,759
If it were the second son,

1077
00:32:19,759 --> 00:32:20,400
would he have the heart?

1078
00:32:21,079 --> 00:32:21,799
If it were the third son,

1079
00:32:22,000 --> 00:32:22,640
would he dare?

1080
00:32:23,079 --> 00:32:24,200
Even with the fourth son-in-law,

1081
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:25,240
he'd think twice!

1082
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:26,640
So why mistreat our family

1083
00:32:26,640 --> 00:32:28,240
with zero hesitation?

1084
00:32:28,519 --> 00:32:29,480
We worked for your dad,

1085
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:31,920
running this crew day and night for him!

1086
00:32:32,599 --> 00:32:34,599
You did all the dirty, grueling work!

1087
00:32:34,839 --> 00:32:35,880
He made plenty of money,

1088
00:32:36,039 --> 00:32:36,759
but how much did he give you?

1089
00:32:37,319 --> 00:32:38,839
3,000 yuan a month for you,

1090
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,319
less than what Yang Qingyou makes!

1091
00:32:40,519 --> 00:32:40,960
And me?

1092
00:32:41,119 --> 00:32:41,920
3,000 for me too.

1093
00:32:42,400 --> 00:32:42,839
And what is that?

1094
00:32:43,519 --> 00:32:44,519
That's for living expenses!

1095
00:32:45,519 --> 00:32:46,960
Deduct the two kids' school fees,

1096
00:32:48,000 --> 00:32:49,119
and we're left with 1,500!

1097
00:32:49,559 --> 00:32:50,240
Outsiders look at us

1098
00:32:50,240 --> 00:32:51,480
and think living with him

1099
00:32:51,480 --> 00:32:52,559
gives us some huge perk!

1100
00:32:52,559 --> 00:32:54,960
We don't have a penny left every month!

1101
00:32:55,359 --> 00:32:56,599
Even for Zhenzhu's tutoring fees,

1102
00:32:56,599 --> 00:32:58,440
I don't know where to scrape up the money!

1103
00:32:58,960 --> 00:32:59,880
Now the family assets are being divided,

1104
00:32:59,880 --> 00:33:02,279
14.28 million in demolition payouts!

1105
00:33:02,599 --> 00:33:04,599
The old man sealed his lips and hid it from us!

1106
00:33:04,839 --> 00:33:06,720
I had to find out from the third brother!

1107
00:33:07,359 --> 00:33:09,119
Deep down, from start to finish,

1108
00:33:09,160 --> 00:33:10,599
that old man never cared about our family!

1109
00:33:11,000 --> 00:33:11,799
Come on, what do you mean

1110
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,279
"our family" or not?

1111
00:33:13,480 --> 00:33:13,759
Look,

1112
00:33:14,400 --> 00:33:15,039
by your logic,

1113
00:33:15,440 --> 00:33:16,000
if we run into trouble,

1114
00:33:16,079 --> 00:33:16,960
Dad would just leave us hanging?

1115
00:33:17,279 --> 00:33:17,960
Zhenzhu's tuition—

1116
00:33:18,079 --> 00:33:18,680
if it's really an issue,

1117
00:33:18,920 --> 00:33:19,519
I'll go ask Dad for it.

1118
00:33:19,519 --> 00:33:20,240
Don't you dare ask him!

1119
00:33:20,559 --> 00:33:20,799
Then...

1120
00:33:20,799 --> 00:33:21,839
I'm so sick of owing him favors!

1121
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:24,200
If groceries cost fifty cents or a dollar more,

1122
00:33:24,200 --> 00:33:25,079
he nags endlessly about it!

1123
00:33:25,599 --> 00:33:26,960
If you bring up tutoring fees,

1124
00:33:27,279 --> 00:33:29,039
he'll give me dirty looks for days!

1125
00:33:29,279 --> 00:33:30,079
So what do you want to do?

1126
00:33:30,359 --> 00:33:30,839
Divide the estate!

1127
00:33:31,400 --> 00:33:32,400
Split his 14 million!

1128
00:33:32,519 --> 00:33:33,279
That money cannot be split.

1129
00:33:35,759 --> 00:33:36,319
Just think about it.

1130
00:33:37,319 --> 00:33:38,039
With that much money,

1131
00:33:39,079 --> 00:33:39,880
the old man won't ever

1132
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:41,279
just let it sit earning interest.

1133
00:33:41,920 --> 00:33:43,119
He'll definitely put it into the construction team

1134
00:33:43,119 --> 00:33:44,480
to expand the business!

1135
00:33:45,039 --> 00:33:46,279
As long as the money is in the construction team,

1136
00:33:46,680 --> 00:33:48,119
it's as good as in our hands.

1137
00:33:48,839 --> 00:33:49,920
Think about it:

1138
00:33:50,319 --> 00:33:51,359
your second brother wants to be an official,

1139
00:33:51,799 --> 00:33:53,240
your fourth sister married into money,

1140
00:33:53,480 --> 00:33:54,000
and what about the third?

1141
00:33:55,279 --> 00:33:56,319
He never does anything proper,

1142
00:33:56,319 --> 00:33:57,200
just slacking off every single day.

1143
00:33:57,640 --> 00:33:58,039
And Xiao Wu?

1144
00:33:59,480 --> 00:34:01,039
I raised Xiao Wu with my own hands.

1145
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,359
Xiao Wu will be living with us anyway.

1146
00:34:02,799 --> 00:34:03,680
So in this family,

1147
00:34:04,079 --> 00:34:05,880
who can compete with us for the construction team?

1148
00:34:06,440 --> 00:34:07,160
Even if they tried,

1149
00:34:07,680 --> 00:34:08,599
who else could actually manage it?

1150
00:34:09,280 --> 00:34:10,440
As long as the family doesn't divide,

1151
00:34:10,440 --> 00:34:11,840
I'm still the eldest sister-in-law here.

1152
00:34:12,199 --> 00:34:13,920
He'll have to hand it to us eventually.

1153
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:15,880
Xiuming, mark my words:

1154
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:17,880
let's just let the third brother kick up a fuss.

1155
00:34:17,880 --> 00:34:19,079
We're not getting tangled up with him.

1156
00:34:19,639 --> 00:34:20,519
Absolutely not.

1157
00:34:21,480 --> 00:34:22,679
Did you hear me?

1158
00:34:24,599 --> 00:34:26,119
Everyone, let's take a quick break.

1159
00:34:26,519 --> 00:34:27,400
We'll continue in a bit.

1160
00:34:33,320 --> 00:34:33,719
Chief Song.

1161
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:37,760
It's fine. You don't have to follow me.

1162
00:34:37,960 --> 00:34:38,719
I'm just going to the restroom.

1163
00:35:06,039 --> 00:35:07,280
Cheng Shihai of Rongsheng Group

1164
00:35:08,440 --> 00:35:10,159
bribed Chief Song at the Port Authority.

1165
00:35:10,800 --> 00:35:11,519
You don't stand a chance.

1166
00:35:12,119 --> 00:35:13,320
Tengyue is just making up the numbers.

1167
00:35:15,639 --> 00:35:16,159
What do you mean?

1168
00:35:16,559 --> 00:35:17,559
Since Director Song took the money,

1169
00:35:18,679 --> 00:35:20,119
it means the bid has already been rigged.

1170
00:35:21,719 --> 00:35:23,079
You work for the Port Authority,

1171
00:35:23,679 --> 00:35:24,039
don't you?

1172
00:35:24,440 --> 00:35:25,639
This is a multibillion-dollar project.

1173
00:35:26,800 --> 00:35:27,760
This is only Phase One.

1174
00:35:28,679 --> 00:35:29,599
Next, there will be Phase Two,

1175
00:35:30,039 --> 00:35:31,239
Phase Three, and Phase Four.

1176
00:35:31,960 --> 00:35:32,760
A project of this scale

1177
00:35:33,199 --> 00:35:34,800
comes along once in a lifetime.

1178
00:35:37,480 --> 00:35:37,800
Fine.

1179
00:35:38,360 --> 00:35:39,039
Then out with it.

1180
00:35:39,559 --> 00:35:40,199
What do you want?

1181
00:35:40,679 --> 00:35:41,119
A promotion?

1182
00:35:41,480 --> 00:35:42,480
Or a kickback?

1183
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:43,880
I just want an opportunity.

1184
00:35:44,360 --> 00:35:46,159
I know Tengyue is looking to outsource legal work.

1185
00:35:46,920 --> 00:35:48,159
I graduated from a top law school,

1186
00:35:48,360 --> 00:35:49,440
majoring in economic law.

1187
00:35:49,840 --> 00:35:51,079
I want to take on Tengyue Group's

1188
00:35:51,079 --> 00:35:52,480
legal representation in Honggang.

1189
00:35:53,320 --> 00:35:54,519
You're a civil servant.

1190
00:35:54,880 --> 00:35:56,679
Providing services to me is illegal.

1191
00:35:57,320 --> 00:35:57,880
Give me the word,

1192
00:35:58,519 --> 00:35:59,199
and I'll resign immediately.

1193
00:36:04,039 --> 00:36:04,840
What do you need me to do?

1194
00:36:05,079 --> 00:36:05,639
When you go back,

1195
00:36:06,159 --> 00:36:06,880
withdraw from the bidding conference.

1196
00:36:07,480 --> 00:36:08,280
Let me finish.

1197
00:36:08,880 --> 00:36:09,760
I know it's a risk.

1198
00:36:10,159 --> 00:36:11,239
You'll forfeit your deposit,

1199
00:36:11,639 --> 00:36:12,840
and sour ties with the Port Authority.

1200
00:36:13,480 --> 00:36:14,039
According to regulations,

1201
00:36:14,400 --> 00:36:16,559
at least three bidders must take part

1202
00:36:16,760 --> 00:36:18,000
for the conference to proceed.

1203
00:36:18,519 --> 00:36:19,039
If you withdraw,

1204
00:36:19,159 --> 00:36:20,239
the bidding will have to be halted.

1205
00:36:20,719 --> 00:36:21,440
If they could get their bribe

1206
00:36:21,440 --> 00:36:23,000
into our little Legal Division,

1207
00:36:23,280 --> 00:36:24,000
what about the other departments?

1208
00:36:24,639 --> 00:36:25,360
Only by halting it

1209
00:36:26,360 --> 00:36:27,119
will you have a chance.

1210
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:37,719
Open the door! Is someone in there?

1211
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:40,840
Anyone in there? Open up!

1212
00:36:49,880 --> 00:36:50,840
Why should I trust you?

1213
00:36:51,360 --> 00:36:52,719
Why should you trust me?

1214
00:36:54,159 --> 00:36:54,920
We're both taking a gamble.

1215
00:37:03,079 --> 00:37:03,840
What's your name?

1216
00:37:06,159 --> 00:37:06,679
My surname is Sai.

1217
00:37:08,199 --> 00:37:08,800
Sai Xiuliang.

1218
00:37:38,159 --> 00:37:38,880
Right away, just a second!

1219
00:37:39,159 --> 00:37:39,920
It's about to start.

1220
00:37:54,039 --> 00:37:54,920
Let's proceed.

1221
00:37:55,280 --> 00:37:55,920
Distinguished leaders,

1222
00:37:56,480 --> 00:37:58,360
given the current status of this tender,

1223
00:37:58,599 --> 00:38:00,800
which deviates from our expectations,

1224
00:38:01,159 --> 00:38:02,159
after careful consideration,

1225
00:38:02,320 --> 00:38:03,679
our company has decided to withdraw.

1226
00:38:04,119 --> 00:38:05,719
We look forward to future collaboration.

1227
00:38:06,320 --> 00:38:06,679
Thank you.

1228
00:38:07,280 --> 00:38:08,320
All our materials are ready!

1229
00:38:08,320 --> 00:38:08,719
Mr. Shi!

1230
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:09,400
What's going on?

1231
00:38:09,519 --> 00:38:09,920
Mr. Shi!

1232
00:38:10,119 --> 00:38:11,119
Why so sudden?

1233
00:38:11,239 --> 00:38:11,639
Mr. Shi!

1234
00:38:11,639 --> 00:38:13,199
Why is Mr. Shi leaving so soon?

1235
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:14,159
What's going on here?

1236
00:38:14,159 --> 00:38:15,000
What happened, Mr. Shi?

1237
00:38:15,079 --> 00:38:15,960
This is an absolute joke!

1238
00:38:47,119 --> 00:38:47,400
Dad,

1239
00:38:47,719 --> 00:38:48,719
do you think this thing

1240
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:49,760
works pretty well?

1241
00:38:49,880 --> 00:38:50,960
City folks all use it.

1242
00:38:50,960 --> 00:38:51,280
Good.

1243
00:38:52,920 --> 00:38:53,400
Let me pour you some.

1244
00:38:53,679 --> 00:38:54,559
Didn't raise you for nothing.

1245
00:38:54,840 --> 00:38:55,880
You know how to care for your old man.

1246
00:38:56,519 --> 00:38:57,800
Isn't that the least I can do?

1247
00:38:59,159 --> 00:38:59,440
Come on.

1248
00:38:59,960 --> 00:39:00,719
Let's have a drink together.

1249
00:39:01,039 --> 00:39:01,559
A toast to you.

1250
00:39:02,360 --> 00:39:02,639
Good.

1251
00:39:08,199 --> 00:39:08,480
Dad,

1252
00:39:09,079 --> 00:39:10,639
I came across a great opportunity recently.

1253
00:39:11,320 --> 00:39:12,440
There's this foreign

1254
00:39:12,599 --> 00:39:13,599
wonder drug for heart disease

1255
00:39:14,320 --> 00:39:15,199
being brought into the country.

1256
00:39:15,480 --> 00:39:16,039
I want to

1257
00:39:16,320 --> 00:39:17,840
land the exclusive distribution rights.

1258
00:39:18,519 --> 00:39:19,599
If this pulls through,

1259
00:39:20,239 --> 00:39:21,239
and I'm not bragging, Dad,

1260
00:39:21,880 --> 00:39:22,440
down the road,

1261
00:39:22,960 --> 00:39:24,039
it'll be a gold mine.

1262
00:39:24,639 --> 00:39:26,119
Our family will never worry about money.

1263
00:39:27,360 --> 00:39:28,000
That's great.

1264
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:28,480
Dad!

1265
00:39:29,559 --> 00:39:29,840
Dad!

1266
00:39:31,039 --> 00:39:31,719
Little brother is back!

1267
00:39:31,719 --> 00:39:32,360
Hey, Big Brother!

1268
00:39:32,880 --> 00:39:33,440
Long time no see.

1269
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:34,800
Jiao,

1270
00:39:35,119 --> 00:39:36,360
get your brother a bowl and chopsticks.

1271
00:39:37,840 --> 00:39:38,119
Dad,

1272
00:39:38,519 --> 00:39:39,360
why are you wearing this again?

1273
00:39:39,480 --> 00:39:40,280
Didn't I tell you?

1274
00:39:40,440 --> 00:39:41,199
It's bad for your nerves.

1275
00:39:41,519 --> 00:39:41,880
Take it off.

1276
00:39:42,239 --> 00:39:43,440
I think it's pretty good.

1277
00:39:43,440 --> 00:39:43,960
Let me tell you,

1278
00:39:43,960 --> 00:39:45,639
I just got back from the third Sai brother's.

1279
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:47,280
Grab me a beer!

1280
00:39:48,719 --> 00:39:49,480
Down in the south of town,

1281
00:39:50,559 --> 00:39:52,159
a new real estate project is taking off.

1282
00:39:52,719 --> 00:39:53,280
The two of us talked it over,

1283
00:39:53,280 --> 00:39:54,159
and we're gonna make a big play.

1284
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:55,440
You might not know,

1285
00:39:55,559 --> 00:39:56,559
but in real estate right now,

1286
00:39:56,679 --> 00:39:57,400
prices change every day.

1287
00:39:57,800 --> 00:39:58,719
Mark my words, within a year,

1288
00:39:58,920 --> 00:39:59,599
it'll definitely double.

1289
00:40:01,280 --> 00:40:01,519
Dad,

1290
00:40:01,679 --> 00:40:02,559
let's celebrate in advance.

1291
00:40:02,880 --> 00:40:03,480
All right, all right.

1292
00:40:03,559 --> 00:40:03,840
Here.

1293
00:40:04,199 --> 00:40:04,559
Come on, Big Brother.

1294
00:40:05,000 --> 00:40:05,320
Bottoms up.

1295
00:40:05,800 --> 00:40:06,079
Here.

1296
00:40:06,239 --> 00:40:06,719
Bottoms up.

1297
00:40:06,800 --> 00:40:07,239
Bottoms up, bottoms up.

1298
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:11,800
Dad,

1299
00:40:12,280 --> 00:40:12,920
this food is great.

1300
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:15,199
You two have really made something of yourselves.

1301
00:40:15,880 --> 00:40:17,000
But you still need to keep pushing forward.

1302
00:40:17,239 --> 00:40:19,199
There's still plenty of room to grow.

1303
00:40:19,239 --> 00:40:19,800
Right?

1304
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:20,400
Absolutely.

1305
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:22,320
I won't hide it from you two.

1306
00:40:23,679 --> 00:40:24,719
The village was demolished,

1307
00:40:26,280 --> 00:40:27,480
and the payout came through.

1308
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:28,800
Our family got...

1309
00:40:29,320 --> 00:40:29,840
nine million.

1310
00:40:31,280 --> 00:40:31,599
Dad,

1311
00:40:31,800 --> 00:40:32,519
this money...

1312
00:40:32,679 --> 00:40:33,199
how do we split it?

1313
00:40:34,320 --> 00:40:35,440
You two brothers talk it over

1314
00:40:35,599 --> 00:40:36,119
and make a decision.

1315
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:37,320
Whatever you say, whatever you say.

1316
00:40:37,960 --> 00:40:38,880
I only have one condition.

1317
00:40:39,199 --> 00:40:40,320
No matter what, you've got to...

1318
00:40:40,800 --> 00:40:42,719
you've got to look out for Jiao.

1319
00:40:43,079 --> 00:40:44,079
She's been divorced for two years,

1320
00:40:44,199 --> 00:40:45,360
and life hasn't been easy for her.

1321
00:40:45,800 --> 00:40:46,639
One is her older brother,

1322
00:40:46,960 --> 00:40:47,840
the other is her younger brother.

1323
00:40:48,079 --> 00:40:48,599
Right?

1324
00:40:54,960 --> 00:40:55,920
Dad, here's what I think.

1325
00:40:55,920 --> 00:40:56,320
Well...

1326
00:40:56,639 --> 00:40:57,559
she did get a divorce,

1327
00:40:57,920 --> 00:40:59,159
but it's not like I made her, right?

1328
00:40:59,360 --> 00:41:00,800
Plus, she kept saying

1329
00:41:01,599 --> 00:41:02,480
her husband was beating her,

1330
00:41:03,519 --> 00:41:04,280
but none of us ever saw it.

1331
00:41:04,440 --> 00:41:05,000
Of course,

1332
00:41:05,079 --> 00:41:06,239
we... we're all family.

1333
00:41:06,400 --> 00:41:07,559
We'll take care of her where we should,

1334
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:08,239
but...

1335
00:41:09,119 --> 00:41:10,639
what's the standard here?

1336
00:41:11,960 --> 00:41:12,320
Dad,

1337
00:41:12,920 --> 00:41:14,480
are you really giving Laijiao a share?

1338
00:41:17,960 --> 00:41:18,719
If you ask me,

1339
00:41:19,480 --> 00:41:20,559
even though Laijiao got divorced,

1340
00:41:20,880 --> 00:41:21,719
strictly speaking,

1341
00:41:21,920 --> 00:41:23,280
she's not part of the Ma family anymore.

1342
00:41:23,960 --> 00:41:25,000
Coming back to take a share of the money...

1343
00:41:25,199 --> 00:41:26,039
isn't that against custom?

1344
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:29,280
If young wives everywhere

1345
00:41:29,519 --> 00:41:31,239
use this trick to come back for money,

1346
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:32,800
won't everything descend into chaos?

1347
00:41:33,119 --> 00:41:33,760
When people say

1348
00:41:34,159 --> 00:41:35,199
the Ma family started this trend,

1349
00:41:35,800 --> 00:41:37,039
do you really think that's right?

1350
00:41:37,480 --> 00:41:39,559
Both born of the same flesh and bone,

1351
00:41:40,159 --> 00:41:42,800
yet split apart when wealth is known.

1352
00:41:43,519 --> 00:41:45,159
Gold and land to sons they hand,

1353
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:48,079
while married daughters outcasted stand.

1354
00:41:49,400 --> 00:41:51,360
How many slights this world has made,

1355
00:41:51,960 --> 00:41:54,960
that cause our bitter tears to shed.

1356
00:42:41,199 --> 00:42:41,840
Uncle.

1357
00:42:42,360 --> 00:42:42,719
Jiao.

1358
00:42:43,960 --> 00:42:44,840
What are you doing here?

1359
00:42:48,079 --> 00:42:49,480
I've been back for two years.

1360
00:42:49,840 --> 00:42:51,000
Had nothing better to do,

1361
00:42:51,000 --> 00:42:51,960
so I came here to help out.

1362
00:42:52,599 --> 00:42:53,679
Earn a little extra cash, too.

1363
00:42:55,400 --> 00:42:56,320
Uncle, are... are you...

1364
00:42:56,480 --> 00:42:58,079
here because you're not feeling well?

1365
00:42:58,400 --> 00:42:58,719
No,

1366
00:42:59,320 --> 00:42:59,840
no.

1367
00:43:00,119 --> 00:43:01,519
I was just wandering around the streets,

1368
00:43:01,760 --> 00:43:02,719
and happened to stroll by.

1369
00:43:02,960 --> 00:43:04,039
Came to ask Old Zheng something.

1370
00:43:04,639 --> 00:43:05,800
I'll go ask him. He's... in...

1371
00:43:06,159 --> 00:43:06,719
He's in this room.

1372
00:43:06,719 --> 00:43:07,119
Right in here.

1373
00:43:07,199 --> 00:43:08,480
You do your work. Don't worry about me.

1374
00:43:08,639 --> 00:43:09,039
Don't mind me.

1375
00:43:10,760 --> 00:43:11,280
Old Zheng...

1376
00:43:20,480 --> 00:43:22,039
Having kids in this life...

1377
00:43:22,159 --> 00:43:24,239
some are just born to collect debts.

1378
00:43:24,320 --> 00:43:25,480
When we have money...

1379
00:43:25,519 --> 00:43:26,079
Money...

1380
00:43:29,039 --> 00:43:29,559
Dacheng.

1381
00:43:31,159 --> 00:43:32,039
The old supervisor left,

1382
00:43:32,280 --> 00:43:33,239
and a young one took over.

1383
00:43:33,840 --> 00:43:35,119
The old one shook us down for bribes,

1384
00:43:35,280 --> 00:43:36,440
while the young one plays it by the book.

1385
00:43:37,159 --> 00:43:38,039
You guys just have rotten luck.

1386
00:43:38,679 --> 00:43:39,840
That old supervisor and the young one

1387
00:43:39,840 --> 00:43:41,000
are actually uncle and nephew.
